WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.225 --> 00:00:08.350
DANIEL VIVEIROS: Hey, guys.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.880
Good morning.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.140
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.070
My name is Daniel.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:16.800
And I'm here today to
tell a story to you.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.360
A story of how we went
from idea to market

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.430
in less than six months.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:28.500
I'm here to share our experience
on creating new products

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.770
with Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:33.710
I have been working with
Google Cloud Platform for more

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.790
than five years, right now.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.670
I'm a Google Developer
expert, by the way.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:43.720
But my main job is being the
head of Product Engineering

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:49.800
at CI&amp;T. CI&amp;T is a Brazilian
company with subsidiaries

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:56.500
in Japan, China, Europe, Canada,
and the United States, as well.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.720
We have a lot of
talented people.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:04.280
And we are really proud to
be elected the Google Cloud

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.860
partner of the year into 2014.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.490
We got this
recognition last year.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.760
And part of this
recognition came from cases

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.450
like this one here, the
Coca-Cola Happiness Flag.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.150
You saw the video today
at the keynote, right?

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:24.250
Coca-Cola Happiness Flag
is a global market campaign

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.110
from Coca-Cola to
FIFA World Cup 2014.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:32.710
The campaign was the World
Cup is for everybody.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:37.340
And the idea was to connect
people all around the world,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:42.070
getting photos to create
this huge photo mosaic called

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:44.270
the Happiness Flag.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.200
We created a system
that engaged the users

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.620
on social networks such as
Facebook, Twitter, Instagram.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.930
We created websites to allow
users to submit photos directly

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.100
to Coca-Cola.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.080
We converted text to image.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.000
We did a lot of things.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.750
And at the end of the campaign,
we had millions of images.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.750
We did everything using
Google App Engine.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.660
For computer workloads, we
stored this massive amount

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.630
of images on Google
Cloud Storage.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:24.110
And we used Google Compute
Engine for specific workloads,

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.680
such as advanced
image transformations.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.840
And the result is here.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.940
The Happiness Flag was unveiled
during the opening of the World

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:35.570
Cup.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:40.580
And the overall campaign
was a huge success.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:47.650
At this point, we felt we had
a very special set of skills.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.810
We had this strong
partnership with Google.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.390
We had great developers-- a lot
of Google certified developers,

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.620
by the way.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.950
We had been working with
machine learning for a while.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:04.190
And we had always been
heavy users of Google Apps

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.520
and Google+.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.960
We knew we could do
something remarkable

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.290
with this special set of skills.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.000
And we did our company website.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.390
Sounds a little bit
frustrating, right?

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.240
Well, not actually.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.530
Our company website is
a very cool website.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.620
It's a card based website.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.510
Very responsive.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.130
It renders in different
kinds of displays.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:34.250
It is social connected, so it's
really easy to get a post from

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.600
Google+, for example, and
leverage that post inside

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.120
our website.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.790
And it's the smart.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:44.770
We are using machine learning
and recommendation systems

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:48.970
to provide a custom
experience for our users.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:52.230
We are putting what is
more relevant on the top

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.770
and what is less
relevant on the bottom.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:59.490
Actually, our
website was so cool

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.980
that our customers wanted it.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:06.550
And we started a new line of
business based on our website.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.380
Today, we have our
website running

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:14.170
on more than 25 companies,
including very large ones.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:19.839
We were excited,
but we still thought

00:04:19.839 --> 00:04:23.360
that we had zero product.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.190
That's because
every time we needed

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:29.260
to deploy a new
version of our website,

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:33.190
we were still taking
from one to three months

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:36.500
to do that because we need
to do a lot of customizations

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.240
in terms of look and feel, a lot
of discussions with marketing

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.250
areas, if card is a good
design strategy or not.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.740
We need to handle
feature requests.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.410
And we wanted a very,
very scalable product

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.290
in terms of business.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:57.230
We wanted a software
as a service product.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:02.420
We wanted to move
from 0 to 1 product.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:08.300
That's why September, 2015,
we ran a design sprint.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.670
A design sprint is a
methodology from Google

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:14.730
that allows you to move from
idea, discuss this idea,

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:18.250
prototype this idea, and
validate this idea with users.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.880
And we did everything.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.320
We did everything by the book.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.950
We got a lot of people
inside another home.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.610
And we converged.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.020
We diverged.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.900
We prototyped ideas.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.920
And we validated those
ideas with users,

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:39.870
customers, prospects.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:42.880
And at the end of
this period, we

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.220
had the vision of
our first product.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:50.790
And we called it Smart Canvas.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.490
And I want to share this
vision with you, right now.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:08.760
Smart Canvas is a system that
allows you to tear down silos,

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.430
to connect people.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.339
And we want to do that
in a very smart way.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:14.297
So we allow our users--

00:06:14.297 --> 00:06:14.435
[VIDEO PLAYBACK]

00:06:14.435 --> 00:06:16.290
-To inspire more
and more knowledge,

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.450
and ignite night great ideas.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:22.570
What if connections could
be made automatically

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:26.990
to propel the most
important thing,

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:31.400
to bring people closer together,
to heighten ideas and solve

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.046
problems, together.

00:06:33.046 --> 00:06:40.854
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:06:40.854 --> 00:06:42.318
[END PLAYBACK]

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.230
DANIEL VIVEIROS: Of
course, at that point,

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:48.390
we just had the idea.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.180
The video came later.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.350
So now, we had the idea.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:55.630
We just need to
build the product.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:58.020
And that's the story I want
to tell you, right now.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:03.240
And to help me tell the story, I
want to introduce you our gang.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.770
They usually help us
with announcements,

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.490
with customer support.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:12.190
Today, they agreed to help me
with this presentation, here.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:14.710
We are going to do a
little role playing game.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.870
So let me introduce you.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.530
First is Lorenzo.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:20.240
Lorenzo if from Italy.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.450
Very sophisticated.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:25.460
He's going to be our UX Expert.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.550
We have Olivia.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.140
Olivia is from Australia.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.660
She's very tough.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:32.060
She's going to be
our Scrum Master.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.900
We have Ajay from
Jamaica-- addicted

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.510
on Android technologies.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.300
He's going to be our
Mobile Developer.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:40.250
We have Liam.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.820
Liam is from the United States.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.540
He loves Chrome,
Polymer, AngularJS,

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.270
all the web technologies.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.850
He's going to be our
Frontend Developer.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:54.480
And we have Tania Tanya's
from Brazil, Rio de Janeiro

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.300
She likes Samba.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.870
And she is a nerd.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.620
Yes, it's possible.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.620
Tania's one of those people.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.920
I'm the second one.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.740
I don't know if we have more.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:10.250
There's just one person
missing, our Hound.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:14.810
Our grumping-- I mean
lovable, Product Manager.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:18.950
And Apollo agreed to play
our Product Manager, today.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:25.120
And he is the first one to
say, OK, we have a deadline.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.930
We needed to get
the product done

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:31.740
by the event, TeamWork 2016.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:36.179
The event TeamWork 2016
is a huge Google event

00:08:36.179 --> 00:08:39.600
that just happened in
Las Vegas two weeks ago.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.520
And Google partners
all around the world

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:47.350
came to Vegas to know the
roadmap, to talk with Googlers,

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:51.130
to network with other partners.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.090
And it was very important.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.340
It was a really good
opportunity for us

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.910
to introduce Smart
Canvas in this event

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:02.760
because we could
get some customers,

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.440
perhaps some reselling
opportunities,

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.910
but for sure, we will be able
to get valuable feedback.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:13.820
Smart Canvas was designed
since the very beginning

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.910
to work very tightly
coupled with Google Apps.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.880
Seamless experience
with Google Apps.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:24.830
So being able to show Smart
Canvas to those partners

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.620
was really a big thing for us.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:32.960
That's why we needed to
move from idea to market

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:35.040
in less than six months.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.190
We needed to hit
the ground running.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:42.300
And when it comes to
hit the ground running,

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.880
I like using Google App Engine.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:49.820
I know that for most of you,
using Google Compute Engine,

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:52.360
using infrastructure
as a service would

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.840
be the first choice.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.600
For me, it would be
to the third choice.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:00.700
I would like to go with
Google App Engine first.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.960
Second would be
Container Engine-- using

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.520
containers deployed on Google.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:08.060
And the third one,
Compute Engine.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:12.990
I like Google App Engine,
not only because it provides

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:15.750
fully abstraction
of infrastructure,

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.400
so we don't have
to worry about load

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.950
balancing, high availability,
stuff like that,

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:24.650
but also because it provides
an architecture for you

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:25.540
to develop.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:29.920
It provides a mechanism, such
as Memcache, task queues.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:34.670
So it's very handy when you
need to hit the ground running.

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:37.580
We used Google App
Engine for Coca-Cola.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:40.260
We used Google App
Engine for our website.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:41.950
We had the expertise.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:46.210
So now, we decided to
use App Engine again.

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:49.210
So Olivia told the
team, guys, we are

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.220
going to use Google App Engine.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:53.880
And that triggered
some reactions, right?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.850
Some people were not very
happy with that decision.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:57.740
Oh, my god.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.070
Is it really flexible?

00:10:59.070 --> 00:10:59.680
I don't know.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.220
I'm afraid of death.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.831
Some people were willing
to use containers.

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:05.330
So, what?

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.370
You're not going
to use containers?

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:08.750
Are you sure of that?

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:12.540
But we got some very
important support

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.500
from our senior developers.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.660
Thank you very much
for the support.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:21.490
And we decided to go
with Google App Engine.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:24.110
In terms of user
interface, Lorenzo

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:27.360
asked us to use Material Design.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:30.200
Material Design is a
no-brainer decision

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.650
when you are talking about
Android Development, rights?

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:37.080
So Ajay was really happy
with that decision.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:42.640
Not that common when you are
talking about web development.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:47.110
You don't see a lot of
websites using Material Design,

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:48.460
right now.

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:53.710
But Polymer has just gotten 1.0.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.750
And we were excited
with the great website

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:00.420
that Google did for
Google I/O 2015.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:03.210
So we decided to use Polymer.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:09.420
And we decided to use Material
Design on all platforms.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:13.990
Well, the backend developers--
they couldn't care less.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:17.700
So that's the first
architecture we got.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.950
Very simple.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.780
We had the frontend here.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:22.810
We had the web using Polymer.

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:24.910
We had Android.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:25.770
We had iOS.

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:31.080
All the clients
consuming services

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.480
served by Google App Engine.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:37.840
We are using Google Datastore
for storing business data.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.870
Again, we could use
Cloud SQL, for example.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:44.090
But we decided to use the
simplest technology, which

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.920
is Datastore.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:49.160
And we are also using
Google Cloud Storage

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:53.010
for storing large files,
such as images for example.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:56.250
And with just that
architecture here,

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:59.440
with just these
components, we were

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:05.030
able to allow our users to
create knowledge, compose

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:10.040
new posts, or bring knowledge
to the product sharing

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.690
external articles,
or bringing Google

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.660
documents to the product.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:18.070
We have this amazing
integration with Google Drive.

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:21.660
We were able to allow our
users to see everything

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:25.502
in a timeline, in a
chronological order are just

00:13:25.502 --> 00:13:30.440
what is targeted [INAUDIBLE]
in the [INAUDIBLE] channel.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:35.140
We allowed our users to create
boards, topics of interest--

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:39.830
very similar to what Pinterest
does, into to curate content

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:42.740
inside the boards.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:45.860
And we allowed them
to share everything

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:49.860
with other people and
other teams, everything

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:53.970
just using these
components here.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:55.900
I'm going to tell
you a little secret.

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:58.810
I'm going to be 100%
honest with you.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.520
These screenshots you
just saw, they were not

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:03.860
from the first release.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.030
They are the current
release, right now.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.670
We polished these screenshots.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:12.780
We polished our user
interface over time.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:16.040
And that was possible
because we saved time

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.530
using Google App Engine.

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:21.290
And that's the value that Google
App Engine brings to the table.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.650
You can start coding right away.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:27.190
You can deliver the first
very versions really fast.

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.730
And you can tweak,
and you can change,

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:34.770
and you can get those feedbacks
and react to them accordingly.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:40.220
So we were up and running.

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:42.730
Let's talk about search.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:46.590
We needed to have a
very, very good search.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:49.410
That makes a lot of sense
because the idea for Smart

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.420
Canvas was to collect as
much content as possible,

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:56.970
either create it inside Smart
Canvas or external content.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:15:00.550
So we would need a
very powerful way

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:04.160
to allow our users to search
for that content later.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:08.050
The first choice here would
be using Google Search API.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.840
We used Google Search
API for our website.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.490
And the results were good.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:18.110
But now, we decided
to use Elasticsearch

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:21.710
because it's more flexible
and, in our opinion,

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:24.260
it's more powerful.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:28.850
The problem here is that you
cannot deploy Elasticsearch

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:30.280
on Google App Engine.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:35.030
Actually, you cannot even access
Elasticsearch using Google App

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:36.210
Engine.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:36.960
Hah.

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:37.640
Yeah.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:40.410
Told me Ajay.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.070
Again, Tania, thank you
very much for the support.

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:47.300
We can always increase
complexity as needed.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:51.070
We can expand our
architecture to accommodate

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:53.480
specific workloads.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.200
You need to be
aware, whenever you

00:15:55.200 --> 00:16:00.260
decide to use a platform
or a fully managed service,

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:05.460
at some point you may need to
create a specific microservice

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.510
to handle specific workloads.

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:09.070
And that's what we did.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:13.310
We used Cloud Launcher to
provision some service,

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:14.780
with Elasticsearch.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.870
It's very handy because,
with a few clicks,

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.520
you can have the
service up and running.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.300
So you should consider that,
at least for the development

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.990
and [INAUDIBLE] environments.

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:26.590
For production
environments, you may

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:29.350
need a more tuned
environment so you

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:31.060
can create your own recipes.

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:34.190
But at least for the development
and [INAUDIBLE] environments,

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:36.970
you should go with
Cloud Launcher.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:40.040
And we created the
Search microservice.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.780
So now, every search
request that comes

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:47.740
from the client to our core,
the core forwards that request

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:49.210
to the Search microservice.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.740
We are using Compute
Engine for that.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.030
We Get the response.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:57.340
And send it back to the clients.

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:59.730
Now, we need to
index the content.

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:01.550
We could use the same approach.

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:05.650
Whenever a new post is
created inside Smart Canvas,

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:07.770
we could just send
that information so

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:12.380
Elasticsearch, for example,
and let it index the content.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.359
We decided to do a
different approach.

00:17:15.359 --> 00:17:20.500
We created an event
broker using Pub-Sub.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.700
And it pays off.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:24.589
I'm going to show
you how we are going

00:17:24.589 --> 00:17:27.819
to expand this idea of
using Pub-Sub, here.

00:17:27.819 --> 00:17:32.200
So whenever something meaningful
happens inside the core,

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:35.230
a new post is created,
a new comment,

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:38.850
a user just liked
a specific post.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:42.980
We get this event and send
that event to Pub-Sub.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:47.430
And Pub-Sub takes care of
distributing this event

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.950
to several microservices.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:51.030
Right now, we just
have Search, here,

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:53.530
but you are going to see
how we evolved this idea.

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:58.570
With that, we were able to
create a very nice search.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:00.750
I love the way
that Elasticsearch

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.730
deals with relevance.

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:05.170
And not only that, we
were able to create

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:07.100
cool features, such
as autocomplete,

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.360
for example, helping
our customers

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.260
to ask for the right questions.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:16.160
So now, our users are
also able to search

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:22.800
for content, for boards, and for
teams with this architecture,

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:24.900
here.

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:29.540
We are now up and running, and
we have the powerful search.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.800
Another request.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:32.550
Social.

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.370
Everything's social, right now.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:36.460
People don't like to
feel that they are alone.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:38.410
We live in a social world.

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:40.650
We are so used
with applications,

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:45.290
with app such as Facebook,
Twitter, WhatsApp, Google+,

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:46.110
whatever.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:51.020
We knew from the very
beginning that Smart Canvas

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:54.210
should be social, as well.

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.900
Lorenzo raised the
bar a little bit.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:19:01.160
OK, I want social, but
I also want real-time.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.300
So we did some basic stuff.

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:07.930
For example, we
created notifications

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:11.820
with a live counter to show
many notifications you have.

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:17.640
We allowed our users to like,
to pin, to bookmark a post,

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:20.110
also with counters.

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:24.180
We have comments, but
we are showing a toast,

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.750
saying, OK, there is a
new comment available.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:28.970
Do you like to comment,
anyway, or do you

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:31.360
like to see that comment first?

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:34.330
That's the kind of real-time
thing I was talking about.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:37.800
And we did something that we
consider very special, which

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:42.490
is, we show on the top of
the post who else is seeing

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:47.020
the same post as you are,
right now, in the same fashion

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:51.080
that google docs does with
documents, presentations,

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:55.210
spreadsheets, and so on.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:56.900
We used Firebase for that.

00:19:56.900 --> 00:20:00.320
Jake came with that idea
and I couldn't agree more.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:03.650
I had always been a
huge fan of Firebase.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:06.710
And I was really happy when
Google acquired the company

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:08.020
two years ago.

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:11.120
And we brought Firebase
to our architecture.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.240
Let me show how we did that.

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:16.630
First, we created another
microservice called

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.500
the real-time microservice.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.740
This time, we are not
using Compute Engine.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:23.960
We are using just another
module inside App Engine.

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:24.900
Why?

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.980
Because it's simpler to do that.

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:30.940
We had no reason to use
Compute Engine here.

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:34.650
And now, Pub-Sub not
only sends all the events

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:38.310
to Search s microservice,
but it also sends the events

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:40.730
to the Real-time microservice.

00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:42.830
With that, we can
just, for example,

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:46.460
send that information to GCM,
to Google Cloud Messaging,

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.370
so our mobile
users can have push

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:50.680
notifications on their devices.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.770
And we can send that
information to Firebase.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:57.250
And it's so simple to do that.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:00.960
With very few lines of code--
three lines of code, here.

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:03.890
This example is using
Java with Jersey.

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:07.140
But I'm pretty sure that any
language of your preference

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:08.990
would be as simple as that.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.990
We can store data
inside Firebase.

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:14.500
What is happening
behind the scenes here--

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.440
we are building a data tree.

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:18.360
So here's example.

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.980
We have tenants because we
are a multi-tenant solution.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:23.610
We have CI&amp;T. It's our tenant.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:24.790
We have posts.

00:21:24.790 --> 00:21:26.690
We have the number of likes.

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:29.000
The number of notifications.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:29.950
Everything.

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:33.920
You just need to model
that information using

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.680
Firebase's best practices.

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:39.400
Here's another example
for the presence alert

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:41.110
I mentioned before.

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.600
That's how to show who
else is seeing the post.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:45.300
Very simple.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.670
Very straightforward.

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:50.810
Now, we need to consume that
information to get these events

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:53.760
and react to them
in the frontend.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:56.470
And it's very simple to do
because Firebase provides

00:21:56.470 --> 00:22:00.360
SDKs for JavaScript,
provides SDKs Android,

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:02.700
provides SDKs for iOS.

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:06.700
So we just need to do
to create the callback

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:08.890
and react to them accordingly.

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:09.900
One example, here.

00:22:09.900 --> 00:22:13.180
If you want to do the something
similar of what it did,

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:15.590
show the avatar
of another person

00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:18.390
that is reading the same
post as you are, right now.

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:22.470
You just need to write a
few lines of JavaScript.

00:22:22.470 --> 00:22:26.280
Here, I'm listening to the
onValue value event, which

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:29.830
is going to be triggered
every time information

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:31.300
changes in the data tree.

00:22:31.300 --> 00:22:33.370
And you just need
to keep a few lists

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:38.180
and show the icon on
the top of the page.

00:22:38.180 --> 00:22:40.580
Very simple, right?

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:43.020
So that's Firebase.

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:47.705
And now, we are also
social and dynamic.

00:22:51.150 --> 00:22:55.080
The core business, the
secret sauce of Smart Canvas

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:59.570
has always been to tear down
silos, to connect people

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:02.640
with content in a smarter way.

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:06.050
So now, it's time to be smart.

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:08.840
And that's my favorite part.

00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:10.360
We want to be smart.

00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:12.190
We want to be magical.

00:23:12.190 --> 00:23:14.320
We want to impact our users.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:16.460
And make them think, oh, my god.

00:23:16.460 --> 00:23:18.740
How do they know that?

00:23:18.740 --> 00:23:23.790
The same way Google has
always been doing with us.

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:28.090
Let me try to explain with you
the initial idea which we think

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:32.080
is very simple,
yet very powerful.

00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:35.060
We wanted to build
this graph, here.

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:37.930
And we wanted to build
it automatically.

00:23:37.930 --> 00:23:41.290
So for example, if
I have a person,

00:23:41.290 --> 00:23:44.540
I want to know what are
the topics of interest

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:45.660
for that person.

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:50.220
And I also want to know what
are the most recommended content

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:52.020
for that specific person.

00:23:52.020 --> 00:23:54.580
If I have a topic,
I want to know who

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:57.120
are the experts of that topic.

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:00.470
And also, what are the
contents more relevant

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:02.500
for this specific topic.

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:04.500
Given the content,
I want to know

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.840
what are the topics
for that content

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:09.200
and who are the
people that would

00:24:09.200 --> 00:24:11.700
be interested in that content.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:15.880
So if you would be able
to create this graph

00:24:15.880 --> 00:24:18.620
and master all
these relationships,

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:22.520
we knew that we could build
something remarkable, something

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:24.720
very, very interesting.

00:24:24.720 --> 00:24:28.800
So we created the Machine
Learning microservice.

00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:33.570
So whenever the core needs
to get some insights to amaze

00:24:33.570 --> 00:24:36.670
the user, it just sends a
request to the Machine Learning

00:24:36.670 --> 00:24:37.610
microservice.

00:24:37.610 --> 00:24:42.030
And we also have some data being
exchanged between the Machine

00:24:42.030 --> 00:24:44.290
Learning and the Pub-Sub.

00:24:44.290 --> 00:24:47.210
But let's drill sound a little
bit in this Machine Learning

00:24:47.210 --> 00:24:49.570
microservice.

00:24:49.570 --> 00:24:53.740
We have App Engine
integrating with Pub-Sub

00:24:53.740 --> 00:24:56.420
and Pub-Sub distributing
all day events--

00:24:56.420 --> 00:25:00.320
a new post, a new comment, a
new link shared, a new board.

00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:03.510
Whatever happens
inside Smart Canvas,

00:25:03.510 --> 00:25:05.000
Pub-Sub is aware of that.

00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:09.840
So now, we are sending all
that information to BigQuery

00:25:09.840 --> 00:25:10.530
as well.

00:25:10.530 --> 00:25:14.560
And we are creating this
huge TouchPoint database

00:25:14.560 --> 00:25:19.100
with everything that
happens inside Smart Canvas.

00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:22.870
Actually, pretty much the same
approach that Spotify is doing.

00:25:22.870 --> 00:25:27.260
We just saw it here
in this morning.

00:25:27.260 --> 00:25:30.690
Now, we need to read data
and crunch that information

00:25:30.690 --> 00:25:31.970
to get these insights.

00:25:31.970 --> 00:25:34.250
And we're using
Dataproc for that.

00:25:34.250 --> 00:25:36.560
Dataproc is a fully
managed service

00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:41.210
from Google that allows you to
run Hadoop and Spark processes.

00:25:41.210 --> 00:25:44.790
And we are using Pi Spark,
to be more specific,

00:25:44.790 --> 00:25:47.270
because we have our
own machine learning

00:25:47.270 --> 00:25:50.190
algorithms written in Python.

00:25:50.190 --> 00:25:53.790
So we are running
everything inside Dataproc.

00:25:53.790 --> 00:25:56.160
And whenever we
have the insights,

00:25:56.160 --> 00:26:00.610
we are writing it on
a Cassandra database.

00:26:00.610 --> 00:26:02.890
We could use Cloud SQL.

00:26:02.890 --> 00:26:07.530
We could use Datastore if you
want to know, for example, oh,

00:26:07.530 --> 00:26:09.450
my god what are
the topics related

00:26:09.450 --> 00:26:12.450
to that person, for
example, or, what

00:26:12.450 --> 00:26:15.060
are the contents for
that specific person.

00:26:15.060 --> 00:26:17.210
If it's something
really simple, we

00:26:17.210 --> 00:26:19.460
could use Cloud
SQL or Datastore.

00:26:19.460 --> 00:26:22.710
But we decided to use
Titan, a graph database that

00:26:22.710 --> 00:26:25.610
runs on the top of
Cassandra because it's

00:26:25.610 --> 00:26:29.450
way more flexible to
run queries on a graph.

00:26:29.450 --> 00:26:32.260
So we can run multiple nodes.

00:26:32.260 --> 00:26:35.060
And it's really,
really powerful.

00:26:35.060 --> 00:26:40.060
So whenever I want to get an
insight to show to my customer,

00:26:40.060 --> 00:26:42.570
App Engine sends a
request to Titan.

00:26:42.570 --> 00:26:45.870
And Titan reads the data
and gets that information

00:26:45.870 --> 00:26:46.990
to App Engine.

00:26:46.990 --> 00:26:50.200
But not only that, we are
pushing that information back

00:26:50.200 --> 00:26:50.700
to Pub-Sub.

00:26:50.700 --> 00:26:53.530
And Pub-Sub can send
that information

00:26:53.530 --> 00:26:55.880
to our search microservice.

00:26:55.880 --> 00:26:59.610
That's really nice because,
now, when a person searches

00:26:59.610 --> 00:27:02.360
for Google, for
example, he's going

00:27:02.360 --> 00:27:06.370
to have content with the
Google keyword on it.

00:27:06.370 --> 00:27:08.880
He's going to have
boards, themes.

00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:14.300
But he also will get person
who is interested in Google.

00:27:14.300 --> 00:27:19.230
He is going to get the experts
of this specific topic.

00:27:19.230 --> 00:27:21.580
Think about your HR area.

00:27:21.580 --> 00:27:24.340
They want to know, for example,
who inside their company

00:27:24.340 --> 00:27:28.230
knows Angular.js or Node.js.

00:27:28.230 --> 00:27:31.020
They can search for
it and can know--

00:27:31.020 --> 00:27:33.760
can get the results of the
persons who are talking

00:27:33.760 --> 00:27:35.690
about that specific subject.

00:27:35.690 --> 00:27:40.400
That's the best way to do
knowledge management because it

00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:43.550
doesn't becomes obsolete.

00:27:43.550 --> 00:27:46.310
So here are some real examples.

00:27:46.310 --> 00:27:49.230
Here's my profile
inside Smart Canvas.

00:27:49.230 --> 00:27:52.690
I put in some information.

00:27:52.690 --> 00:27:55.480
I said that I like
cloud computing, Google,

00:27:55.480 --> 00:27:56.610
Smart Canvas.

00:27:56.610 --> 00:27:59.330
But the algorithms
also discovered

00:27:59.330 --> 00:28:02.510
that I'm interested in
Cloud Platform, nuvem,

00:28:02.510 --> 00:28:04.470
which is cloud in Portuguese.

00:28:04.470 --> 00:28:07.450
And poker, I was in
Vegas two weeks ago.

00:28:10.030 --> 00:28:11.290
People related to you.

00:28:11.290 --> 00:28:13.770
People who are talking
about the same things

00:28:13.770 --> 00:28:15.190
that you are right now.

00:28:15.190 --> 00:28:16.500
So I'm in Brazil.

00:28:16.500 --> 00:28:18.580
I'm interested in Google.

00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:21.640
I may have a coworker
in China that's

00:28:21.640 --> 00:28:23.490
also interested in Google.

00:28:23.490 --> 00:28:25.480
Why not put us in contact.

00:28:25.480 --> 00:28:28.700
That's what we mean
by tear down silos.

00:28:28.700 --> 00:28:32.340
That's what we mean
by connect people.

00:28:32.340 --> 00:28:36.210
And we can have this
vision also per topic.

00:28:36.210 --> 00:28:40.550
So for example, because
I'm interested in Google,

00:28:40.550 --> 00:28:42.700
we have some people
related to you.

00:28:42.700 --> 00:28:45.330
Because you are
interested in digital,

00:28:45.330 --> 00:28:47.980
we have some people
related to you.

00:28:47.980 --> 00:28:52.350
And we also have a channel
that we call Discover that

00:28:52.350 --> 00:28:53.990
shows posts relevant for you.

00:28:53.990 --> 00:28:58.070
So because you like Cloud,
there is brand new information

00:28:58.070 --> 00:28:59.080
here for you.

00:28:59.080 --> 00:29:03.700
Because you are reading about
Google, about Material Design,

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:06.900
I have some posts
for you, as well.

00:29:06.900 --> 00:29:11.440
That's the best way to be
updated what's going on

00:29:11.440 --> 00:29:14.920
inside your organization.

00:29:14.920 --> 00:29:16.210
So that's machine learning.

00:29:16.210 --> 00:29:18.930
And now, we are also smart.

00:29:21.810 --> 00:29:23.960
The cherry on the
top of the cake.

00:29:23.960 --> 00:29:26.170
We had our web application.

00:29:26.170 --> 00:29:28.210
We have some mobile apps.

00:29:28.210 --> 00:29:30.600
We could access those
to get information.

00:29:30.600 --> 00:29:35.120
But now, we want to make the
information find the person.

00:29:35.120 --> 00:29:38.280
We want to cast content
from Smart Canvas

00:29:38.280 --> 00:29:40.090
to external displays.

00:29:40.090 --> 00:29:42.410
We want to explore.

00:29:42.410 --> 00:29:45.710
We want to innovate on
top of Smart Canvas.

00:29:45.710 --> 00:29:49.000
And that's where
Pub-Sub pays off.

00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:53.540
It's very, very simple
to create experiments

00:29:53.540 --> 00:29:55.700
using Pub-Sub because
you just create

00:29:55.700 --> 00:29:57.860
another few subscriptions.

00:29:57.860 --> 00:30:00.510
And you can get all the
data, all the events,

00:30:00.510 --> 00:30:03.880
and do whatever
you want with that.

00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:06.760
And it's so simple that
just one developer is

00:30:06.760 --> 00:30:08.630
able to do that in a few days.

00:30:08.630 --> 00:30:12.140
So Liam took care
of that for us.

00:30:12.140 --> 00:30:16.700
We just created what
we call Co-Cast,

00:30:16.700 --> 00:30:18.610
another microservice add-on.

00:30:18.610 --> 00:30:20.120
Whatever you want to call it.

00:30:20.120 --> 00:30:21.330
And here it is.

00:30:21.330 --> 00:30:25.420
Whenever a new post is
created inside Smart Canvas,

00:30:25.420 --> 00:30:27.890
the information goes to Pub-Sub.

00:30:27.890 --> 00:30:32.110
Pub-Sub sends that information
to the add-on, to Co-Cast.

00:30:32.110 --> 00:30:36.470
And Co-Cast takes care of
showing that information

00:30:36.470 --> 00:30:37.280
in a television.

00:30:37.280 --> 00:30:41.230
Today, at CN&amp;T, we have
several televisions

00:30:41.230 --> 00:30:46.230
showing what's going on
inside our Smart Canvas.

00:30:46.230 --> 00:30:49.370
We used Container
Engine for that.

00:30:49.370 --> 00:30:51.380
Just for fun.

00:30:51.380 --> 00:30:55.580
Actually, just for fun, we think
that Container is a very, very

00:30:55.580 --> 00:30:57.400
strategic technology.

00:30:57.400 --> 00:31:01.210
I personally see, in the
near future-- I don't know,

00:31:01.210 --> 00:31:05.590
few months or a few years--
great chunk of Smart Canvas

00:31:05.590 --> 00:31:07.550
running inside Containers.

00:31:07.550 --> 00:31:12.490
So trying to explore, trying
to get to know the container's

00:31:12.490 --> 00:31:17.110
technology right now-- it seems
to be a good opportunity for us

00:31:17.110 --> 00:31:19.054
to get these [INAUDIBLE]
necessary to works

00:31:19.054 --> 00:31:19.720
with containers.

00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:23.360
So we did that on
Container Engine.

00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:24.850
Just another example.

00:31:24.850 --> 00:31:26.970
We decided to
integrate with Slack.

00:31:26.970 --> 00:31:29.370
Slack is getting momentum--
not getting momentum.

00:31:29.370 --> 00:31:32.890
He has already gotten it.

00:31:32.890 --> 00:31:36.650
So whenever you create a new
post inside Smart Canvas,

00:31:36.650 --> 00:31:39.120
you have this post
coming to Slack, as well.

00:31:39.120 --> 00:31:41.500
So that's it.

00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:43.350
So now we are Smart, magical.

00:31:43.350 --> 00:31:46.600
But we also explore
and innovate.

00:31:46.600 --> 00:31:49.440
And here are the results.

00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:52.160
We went to Las Vegas
a couple of weeks ago.

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:55.160
We had the opportunity to
talk about Smart Canvas

00:31:55.160 --> 00:31:59.560
with partners, with
customers, with Googlers.

00:31:59.560 --> 00:32:03.160
We had the opportunity to
talk about it on stage.

00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:05.650
And we got another recognition.

00:32:05.650 --> 00:32:09.320
We were elected the
Most Googley Partner

00:32:09.320 --> 00:32:11.300
of the year, which
means that we are

00:32:11.300 --> 00:32:15.180
really committed to
Google, to Material Design,

00:32:15.180 --> 00:32:16.540
to all Google technologies.

00:32:16.540 --> 00:32:17.700
We are Alpha Testers.

00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:18.740
We are Beta Testers.

00:32:18.740 --> 00:32:20.830
We strongly believe in GCP.

00:32:23.422 --> 00:32:24.380
And that's [INAUDIBLE].

00:32:24.380 --> 00:32:27.310
Just recapping, we
are up and running.

00:32:27.310 --> 00:32:29.550
Use the fully managed services.

00:32:29.550 --> 00:32:31.500
Use Google API Engine.

00:32:31.500 --> 00:32:35.480
Start simple and increase
complexity as needed.

00:32:35.480 --> 00:32:37.420
Whenever you want
increased complexity.

00:32:37.420 --> 00:32:38.990
That's what we did with search.

00:32:38.990 --> 00:32:42.310
You can always
create a microservice

00:32:42.310 --> 00:32:44.800
to handle specific workloads.

00:32:44.800 --> 00:32:45.760
Be social.

00:32:45.760 --> 00:32:46.670
Be dynamic.

00:32:46.670 --> 00:32:48.740
But also be real-time.

00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:51.630
We have Firebase for that.

00:32:51.630 --> 00:32:52.220
Be Smart.

00:32:52.220 --> 00:32:53.090
Be magical.

00:32:53.090 --> 00:32:56.010
We have several offerings
from Google, right now.

00:32:56.010 --> 00:32:57.370
We have Cloud Machine Learning.

00:32:57.370 --> 00:32:58.230
You just saw it.

00:32:58.230 --> 00:32:58.969
Cloud Vision.

00:32:58.969 --> 00:33:00.010
We are working with that.

00:33:00.010 --> 00:33:02.300
We are playing with
that, right now, as well.

00:33:02.300 --> 00:33:05.470
You can create your own
machine learning algorithms

00:33:05.470 --> 00:33:09.110
using the whole set
of big data tools

00:33:09.110 --> 00:33:10.750
that Google offers to you.

00:33:10.750 --> 00:33:12.320
And explore.

00:33:12.320 --> 00:33:13.000
Innovate.

00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:15.740
Create great things,
amazing things,

00:33:15.740 --> 00:33:19.900
the next things using
the Google technologies.

00:33:19.900 --> 00:33:21.540
We are in private
beta, right now.

00:33:21.540 --> 00:33:24.140
If you go to
smartcanvas.com, you

00:33:24.140 --> 00:33:27.680
can submit your interest
in trying Smart Canvas

00:33:27.680 --> 00:33:32.550
and I will be more than happy
to whitelist your domain.

00:33:32.550 --> 00:33:36.970
I will be around to answer
questions, if you want to.

00:33:36.970 --> 00:33:37.920
And that's it.

00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:38.430
Thank you.

00:33:38.430 --> 00:33:41.480
[APPLAUSE]

